{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And you shall overlay it with pure gold.</b> Rabbi Ibn Ezra made an allusion from the word ״זָהָב״ concerning the blessing over food: ז — this is the blessing of the Sustainer; ה — this is the blessing of the earth; ב — the blessing of the Builder. ״And you shall make for it a crown of gold round about״ (Exodus 25:25) — with everything that HaShem provides him to eat from a high table, he should imagine himself as though he were a king, with a crown that the attribute of contentment has crowned him with. And so our Sages, of blessed memory, said (Avot 6:5): ״And do not lust for the table of kings, for your table is greater than their table, and your crown is greater than their crown.״"], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:23:08.123775604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}